Name:Rules pilot 536 - First strike doesn't help a fight
Goal:Win
Turns:1
Difficulty:Medium
Description:It is your first main phase. You control White Knight (2/2 first strike, protection from black) and have Brute Force and Prey Upon in hand, with one red and one green mana floating. The opponent is at 5 life and controls an untapped Grizzly Bears. Reduce the opponent to 0 life this turn.
Rule:authored-fight-not-combat | Fighting is not combat, so first strike doesn't matter and both creatures deal damage at once (CR 701.14b): Brute Force the Knight first, then it fights and kills the Bears and survives as a 5/5 to attack for 5; fighting first trades the 2/2s, and attacking without Prey Upon lets the Bears block
